        <body>
            <div xml:id="d296-a13">

                <pb facs="0355" n="1089" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1089"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 12 in No. 74.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Breckinridge to Mr. Lewis.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-05-10"><hi rendition="#italic">May 10,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am in receipt of your letter of April 23,
                    in relation to John Ginzberg, who has been under arrest in Minsk, and stating
                    that he desires to return to the United States. You also state the interesting
                    fact, in a case of this character, that he was a minor when he moved or was
                    taken to the United States, being at that time, some fifteen years ago, only 14
                    years of age. I have just written to Ginzberg and will further follow up his
                    case. I don’t think I ever knew of a man who more persistently disregarded the
                    advice he sought, or seemingly tried harder to get into prison than Ginzberg.
                    After a deal of work he is at last out of prison, and has been since the 16th of
                    January, and I hope will get the consent of the Russian Government, which denies
                    the right of expatriation, to return to America.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clifton R. Breckinridge.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
